eview the other PieCharts.\n\n\n**Confirming Chart Centering**\n\nI\'m now implementing the centered `Pie` chart visualization, by setting `cy=\"50%\"` and placing a custom HTML legend below. I\'ve re-examined the chart styles. The \"Status de SLA\" chart\'s properties ( `cy=\"50%\"` and `innerRadius={65}` and `outerRadius={85}` ) are already well set. For the \"Incidentes\" chart, I will ensure its `Pie` component also has `cy=\"50%\"` with `innerRadius={60}` and `outerRadius={80}` and remove its native `<Legend />`. I will position the new HTML legend neatly underneath.\n\n\n**Implementing Pie Chart Center**\n\nI\'ve implemented the `cy=\"50%\"` change for centering the \"Incidentes\" pie chart, and removed its Recharts `<Legend>`. This ensures vertical and horizontal centering within the `ResponsiveContainer`. I will now position the custom HTML legend below the SVG, right under the chart, which I have styled with flex properties to wrap and display the legend neatly. I have made sure to set the `innerRadius` and `outerRadius` of each chart component.\n\n\n**Refining Legend Placement**\n\nI\'ve incorporated a custom HTML legend below the pie chart, styled to display responsively without affecting the chart\'s centering, which is at `cy=\"50%\"`. I\'ve re-reviewed the layout and confirmed a height of `h-72`. I\'m now considering reducing the container\'s height to a fixed value (e.g., `h-52` or `h-56`) to create clean spacing for the legend, or potentially keeping the full layout. I am excited at this point!\n\n\n**Evaluating Legend Height**\n\nI\'m now refining the legend placement to improve its visual appeal and ensure sufficient separation from the `PieChart`. I\'ve assessed that I need to determine the specific height value, and I\'m currently looking at reducing the height of the container that includes the chart and legend from its current value. I\'ve been considering heights of `h-52` and `h-56` or similar. I am excited to see this complete!\n\nI\'ve succ